  - host: github.com
    token: ghp_M5......

When a developer wants to create a new fast-api app, the can select the template for it, and get a form where they fill out the parameters:

application name: default - "my-rest-api"
org (git hub org): default - "rhdh-developers"
it will use the internal image registry

Once the form is sumbitted, developer hub will:
 
 - create new repos in the org based on the application name: <application name>-code (with tekton pipeline webhooks to trigger a build on commit/push) and <application mame>-k8
 - create a namespace that is <application name>
 - deploy the application with argoCD
 - create the pipeline and start a pipeline run
 - create a new catalog component for the rest-api
 - provide a link to the catalog component

 the catalog component will display a number of tabs that have already been configured with dynamic plugins, along with a link to the source code (in github), and a link to the deployment manifests (in git hub), as well as a link to dev spaces. 

